WEBVTT

00:05.964 --> 00:09.175
[opening theme music playing]

00:36.244 --> 00:38.246
[ominous music playing]

01:19.579 --> 01:20.705
[thunder rumbles]

01:24.209 --> 01:25.460
[rain patters]

01:28.296 --> 01:29.798
[woman] You poor things.

01:30.590 --> 01:32.884
Here child, take this and eat.

01:32.967 --> 01:34.135
Oh, my dear!

01:42.185 --> 01:43.728
I'll get you some more to eat.

01:44.312 --> 01:45.480
Please take your time.

01:47.065 --> 01:48.900
[munching]

01:56.991 --> 01:58.034
[child laughs]

02:02.455 --> 02:04.457
[ominous music playing]

02:09.671 --> 02:10.672
[growls]

02:16.553 --> 02:18.054
[door creaking]

02:26.479 --> 02:27.313
Mom.

02:29.357 --> 02:30.191
[growls]

02:30.275 --> 02:31.776
[shrieks in terror]

02:32.986 --> 02:34.988
[suspenseful music playing]

02:45.748 --> 02:46.666
[yells]

02:57.802 --> 02:59.387
[shrieks]

03:11.649 --> 03:12.817
[screams in pain]

03:15.069 --> 03:17.447
[growls, breathes heavily]

03:20.199 --> 03:21.284
- [door opens]
- [woman] Geon!

03:23.578 --> 03:24.787
[soft music playing]

03:24.871 --> 03:27.874
You were to come to me if anything changed
to the body I put his soul into.

03:27.957 --> 03:29.459
How could you let things get like this?

03:29.542 --> 03:32.295
If he devouts another soul,
he can go back to normal.

03:32.378 --> 03:33.880
You have to give him a chance.

03:33.963 --> 03:35.757
Your son has run wild.
He can't be controlled.

03:39.761 --> 03:41.346
I'll have to take back his soul.

03:41.429 --> 03:43.848
[gasps] You can't! You can't.

03:43.932 --> 03:46.392
You're the one
who turned my son into a soul shifter.

03:46.476 --> 03:48.645
Either find a body
for his soul to go into,

03:48.728 --> 03:50.897
or find someone
whose energy he can consume.

03:51.731 --> 03:52.815
Please, save him!

03:53.316 --> 03:54.984
You have to save my baby boy!

03:55.902 --> 03:57.987
If anyone finds out I used this sorcery,

03:59.030 --> 04:00.657
the two of us will be finished.

04:01.407 --> 04:02.325
No!

04:02.951 --> 04:03.826
No!

04:05.578 --> 04:07.205
[crying]

04:09.666 --> 04:10.541
Geon.

04:11.417 --> 04:14.087
Please, hold on! Just a little longer!

04:14.629 --> 04:15.505
Honey.

04:20.843 --> 04:22.845
- [ominous music playing]
- [growls]

04:49.163 --> 04:51.165
[dramatic music playing]

05:01.926 --> 05:03.261
[body cracking]

05:10.476 --> 05:12.437
[slow emotional music playing]

05:19.944 --> 05:20.945
[body thuds]

05:28.119 --> 05:31.831
[Mu] When a soul shifter loses control,
why do their bodies turn to stone?

05:31.914 --> 05:35.084
When the switched body
and the souls clash, a crack forms.

05:36.252 --> 05:38.338
And the body starts losing its energy.

05:38.921 --> 05:41.174
This will make eight soul shifters
who've already run wild.

05:42.133 --> 05:44.385
I think I need to
stop performing the alchemy of souls.

05:45.178 --> 05:46.971
I think you need to
immediately go to the royal palace.

05:48.222 --> 05:51.768
His Highness has requested
information regarding the new spell

05:51.851 --> 05:53.311
that you've been working on.

05:54.520 --> 05:56.522
[ominous music playing]

06:17.627 --> 06:18.544
[Seong inhales harshly]

06:19.253 --> 06:20.088
[coughs]

06:24.258 --> 06:25.426
[Seong coughing]

06:28.471 --> 06:29.472
I've heard…

06:30.556 --> 06:33.017
you've been trying to master a new spell.

06:33.893 --> 06:35.478
Just some part of the tricks for fun,

06:35.561 --> 06:37.563
it's hardly something
I would call a spell.

06:38.189 --> 06:41.025
I know that I can not wish
to live any longer.

06:41.526 --> 06:42.693
However,

06:42.777 --> 06:45.947
I can only regret that I have no heir.

06:46.781 --> 06:48.783
I will pray that
you recover your strength.

06:49.575 --> 06:52.078
[Seong] It is too late
for this sickly body.

06:52.870 --> 06:54.914
If I could just leave it,

06:56.165 --> 06:59.794
and find another that was younger
and healthier than my own.

07:01.879 --> 07:04.715
How could a person possibly change
the body they were born into?

07:08.010 --> 07:10.012
But you're able to do it, can't you?

07:14.350 --> 07:15.935
The alchemy of souls.

07:20.606 --> 07:22.692
[tense music playing]

07:23.985 --> 07:25.862
The alchemy of soul is forbidden magic.

07:25.945 --> 07:28.781
If the soul and body clash,
one could transform into a demon.

07:29.323 --> 07:30.491
Into whose body

07:30.992 --> 07:33.536
would I even dare
to place Your Majesty's soul?

07:33.619 --> 07:36.038
What if you place my soul into your body?

07:36.914 --> 07:38.624
[dramatic music playing]

07:39.208 --> 07:41.210
Not for long. Just seven days.

07:41.752 --> 07:43.671
Switch souls for a week.

07:46.841 --> 07:49.760
I heard that even a soul
that you place into a corpse…

07:50.720 --> 07:53.014
could live in it
for more than half a year.

07:54.557 --> 07:58.728
Between the soul of a king
and the body of his greatest mage,

07:58.811 --> 08:00.313
what is there to worry about?

08:01.522 --> 08:04.901
After seven days,
then you can go and undo this spell.

08:08.196 --> 08:09.947
Now that you've mastered
the alchemy of souls,

08:10.031 --> 08:12.742
something that only
the greatest mages can do,

08:14.035 --> 08:17.914
why waste your time
transplanting souls into decaying corpses?

08:22.752 --> 08:23.961
Jang Gang.

08:24.670 --> 08:26.339
Shift your soul into your king.

08:26.881 --> 08:28.841
[tense music playing]

08:45.816 --> 08:47.568
[epic music playing]

09:27.066 --> 09:28.192
[thunder rumbles]

09:36.784 --> 09:38.786
[epic music continues playing]

10:39.472 --> 10:40.389
[gasps]

10:41.349 --> 10:43.017
[breathes heavily]

10:48.939 --> 10:49.774
[coughing]

11:06.791 --> 11:09.335
His Majesty's soul
and mine have been shifted.

11:14.298 --> 11:15.341
[exhales]

11:18.594 --> 11:20.388
[Seong] I have gone to be with Do-hwa.

11:20.888 --> 11:23.432
When she bears a child,
know that it is mine.

11:25.935 --> 11:26.769
Do-hwa.

11:31.607 --> 11:32.525
Do-hwa.

11:34.193 --> 11:35.653
You truly are beautiful.

11:35.736 --> 11:37.738
[dramatic music playing]

11:46.872 --> 11:48.999
No, you can't do that!

11:50.167 --> 11:51.210
[grunts]

11:51.293 --> 11:52.128
[chokes]

11:53.921 --> 11:56.757
Don't do this to me!
You can't do this to me!

11:57.425 --> 11:58.634
[shouts] You can't!

12:16.610 --> 12:18.612
[upbeat music playing]

12:20.239 --> 12:23.409
[Jang Uk] The energy of the sky
which reigns over the wind,

12:23.492 --> 12:24.952
the rain, the clouds,

12:25.035 --> 12:26.078
touched the land

12:27.037 --> 12:29.457
and created a massive surge of energy.

12:29.540 --> 12:33.002
And with Lake Gyeongcheondaeho
keeping it contained at its center, 

12:33.085 --> 12:34.044
a country was built.

12:34.545 --> 12:38.757
Because of the country's great lake,
the nation was named Daeho.

12:40.050 --> 12:43.429
There are people who can control
the energy of heaven and earth,

12:43.512 --> 12:45.264
and they were called mages.

12:47.099 --> 12:50.352
This tale is a story
about the mages of Daeho,

12:50.436 --> 12:53.647
a place that cannot be found
in history or with a map.

12:58.277 --> 13:00.279
[mysterious music playing]

13:08.370 --> 13:12.041
20 YEARS LATER

13:21.467 --> 13:22.885
So Naksu, the Shadow Assassin

13:22.968 --> 13:25.054
who's been cutting down
mages across the city

13:25.679 --> 13:26.597
is really you.

13:27.097 --> 13:31.060
Everywhere I go,
heads roll, so that's why I chose

13:31.143 --> 13:32.144
"Naksu".

13:33.062 --> 13:34.772
A beautiful name, is it not?

13:35.981 --> 13:37.024
Fire.

13:39.485 --> 13:40.361
Fire!

13:40.444 --> 13:42.446
[dramatic music playing]

14:50.723 --> 14:51.891
[arrows swooshing]

15:00.816 --> 15:02.860
[dramatic music continues playing]

15:55.079 --> 15:56.747
[grunts softly]

16:38.664 --> 16:40.124
We can't let her escape.

16:40.791 --> 16:42.292
- Capture her.
- [mages] Yes, sir!

16:42.376 --> 16:44.378
[ominous music playing]

16:50.634 --> 16:51.593
[exhales roughly]

16:52.219 --> 16:53.637
[footsteps approaching]

16:55.180 --> 16:56.807
[mage 1] This way. Come on.

16:57.474 --> 16:59.476
[tense music playing]

17:07.443 --> 17:08.527
She's over there!

17:09.862 --> 17:10.696
[Naksu grunts]

17:11.321 --> 17:12.156
[mage 3 grunts]

17:12.656 --> 17:13.490
[mage 3 shouts]

17:13.574 --> 17:14.783
[mage 4 grunts, yells]

17:25.085 --> 17:26.086
[mage 5 grunts]

17:26.754 --> 17:27.588
[mage 6 shouts]

17:28.130 --> 17:28.964
[mage 7 shouts]

17:30.132 --> 17:31.091
[mage 8 yells]

17:32.217 --> 17:33.385
[groans]

17:38.348 --> 17:39.183
[Naksu grunts]

17:48.067 --> 17:49.068
[Naksu breathes heavily]

17:53.447 --> 17:55.032
[breathes shakily]

17:58.368 --> 17:59.620
I can't die this way.

18:01.038 --> 18:01.955
Not like this!

18:08.796 --> 18:10.255
[customer 1] Uh, long time no see!

18:10.339 --> 18:12.257
[customer 2] Come on!
Look at his face. Bummer!

18:12.341 --> 18:13.801
[customer 1] What are you drinking?

18:15.094 --> 18:16.637
[indistinct chatter]

18:18.931 --> 18:20.140
[breathes heavily]

18:20.224 --> 18:21.558
- [Mu-deok yelps]
- [Naksu exhales]

18:21.642 --> 18:23.018
[men yelp]

18:23.102 --> 18:24.311
[customer 1] For God's sake!

18:25.687 --> 18:26.814
[customer 2] What's her problem?

18:28.107 --> 18:29.274
[man] Hey, hey, hey!

18:30.400 --> 18:31.652
What are you doing?

18:32.528 --> 18:33.737
[woman panting]

18:36.281 --> 18:37.699
[panting continues]

18:37.783 --> 18:39.785
[mysterious music playing]

19:02.432 --> 19:03.725
TAVERN

19:11.316 --> 19:12.484
[Sang-ho] She is already dead.

19:12.568 --> 19:14.570
[spooky music playing]

19:23.745 --> 19:24.830
[gasps]

19:26.498 --> 19:27.958
[breathes heavily]

19:33.797 --> 19:35.549
There's no blue mark of a soul shifter.

19:39.344 --> 19:41.930
But there are still signs
of her soul leaving.

19:43.307 --> 19:44.641
The alchemy of souls…

19:45.934 --> 19:47.186
was not successful.

19:50.647 --> 19:52.649
[suspenseful music playing]

20:16.256 --> 20:21.094
SONGRIM

20:21.178 --> 20:22.596
[door creaking]

20:24.556 --> 20:25.432
[mage] One.

20:27.893 --> 20:28.727
Two.

20:30.479 --> 20:31.313
Three.

20:31.396 --> 20:32.397
[water hissing]

20:49.206 --> 20:50.082
[Heo Yeom] Hmm.

20:50.916 --> 20:53.460
Yul, come and take a look.

20:57.673 --> 20:58.674
Is this Naksu?

21:00.050 --> 21:00.884
Correct.

21:02.427 --> 21:05.097
[Heo Yeom]
This here is the mark of a soul shifter.

21:06.139 --> 21:09.017
Now, take note!
When the alchemy of souls is performed,

21:09.101 --> 21:12.813
right above the heart,
there will be a blue bruise like this.

21:13.897 --> 21:16.817
If she is the alchemy of souls,
does that mean she's still out there?

21:16.900 --> 21:20.404
It seems that she did cast the spell,
but it must have failed.

21:21.029 --> 21:23.282
While there are traces
of the soul leaving the body,

21:23.365 --> 21:27.244
there weren't any signs that she shifted
into the girl's body that she captured.

21:28.495 --> 21:30.330
[soft music playing]

21:37.379 --> 21:38.255
It's a whistle.

21:38.922 --> 21:39.798
[Heo Yeom] A whistle?

21:39.881 --> 21:42.801
Long ago when I had pet birds,
I used a whistle like this.

21:44.720 --> 21:47.139
Did this woman own a pet bird?

21:47.222 --> 21:49.224
Looks like she's carried it
with her for quite a while.

21:49.975 --> 21:51.810
[Heo Yeom] Seems to be
pretty important to her.

21:52.436 --> 21:57.149
Even an assassin who roams around
beheading people with ease is still human.

21:57.232 --> 22:00.235
She must have had
quite the story of her own.

22:08.118 --> 22:10.579
Naksu's body has already
been seen by many people.

22:10.662 --> 22:13.040
Soon, everyone will be talking
about the alchemy of souls.

22:13.707 --> 22:16.877
Has it been 20 years
since the last soul shifter?

22:16.960 --> 22:17.919
Yes, it has.

22:18.587 --> 22:22.883
Mm. That soul shifter who ran wild
and killed all those people…

22:23.759 --> 22:27.054
I am beginning to fear
something like that will happen again.

22:27.679 --> 22:29.139
[Dang-gu] Uncle!
[gasps]

22:29.222 --> 22:30.057
Uncle.

22:30.974 --> 22:31.808
[Dang-gu panting]

22:31.892 --> 22:34.644
Uncle, is it true Naksu's a soul shifter?

22:35.228 --> 22:37.147
Master! Master Heo, did you see it too?

22:37.230 --> 22:40.692
You're a little excited, aren't you?
Especially to spread some rumor around?

22:40.776 --> 22:43.445
The rumors are already spreading.
Everyone's talking about it.

22:44.112 --> 22:45.906
- Where from?
- At Chwiseonru.

22:45.989 --> 22:47.699
So, instead of training
like you should be,

22:47.783 --> 22:49.618
this Jeongjingak's mage
has just been hanging around

22:49.701 --> 22:51.578
and visiting taverns
and engaging with rumors.

22:51.661 --> 22:53.038
[Heo Yeom chuckles]

22:53.121 --> 22:57.417
Well, Songrim Jeongjingak can be
an excellent place for mages to train.

22:57.501 --> 23:00.462
It can also be a great place
to gather information.

23:00.545 --> 23:05.258
Furthermore, Dang-gu would be next in line
to take your place as Songrim's leader,

23:05.342 --> 23:07.427
and the business man
who will lead our home.

23:07.511 --> 23:09.304
- He'll need to know how to drink.
- Mm.

23:09.387 --> 23:10.472
So, now, you tell me.

23:11.056 --> 23:14.226
What drink at Chwiseonru
do you think is best?

23:14.309 --> 23:17.395
Honestly, I don't go there much
since Uk isn't there.

23:17.479 --> 23:19.898
"Uk"? Jang Uk, the son of Jang Gang?

23:19.981 --> 23:23.944
But isn't he learning Jujang scribe
at a bookstore that's in Yeongchundang?

23:24.027 --> 23:26.113
It's been forever
since he's been kicked out of there.

23:26.196 --> 23:28.115
He's over in Gisan, still. I believe.

23:28.198 --> 23:31.910
Training under the Monk Ho-yeon.
I'm the one who sent him there.

23:32.702 --> 23:37.290
Oh! So, Jang Uk, this time,
is training in a temple now.

23:38.708 --> 23:41.378
Today will be
my last day of training here.

23:43.046 --> 23:45.549
[monk] You are nowhere
near finished with your training.

23:45.632 --> 23:48.927
How dare a student speak of
ending his studies in front of his master.

23:49.010 --> 23:50.846
You told me I need to fill
my head with knowledge,

23:50.929 --> 23:53.306
so I memorized every
single word of hundreds of spell books.

23:53.390 --> 23:55.058
You told me to sharpen my mind,

23:55.142 --> 23:57.769
so I sharpened hundreds of knives
until the whetstone wore down.

23:57.853 --> 24:01.773
But you never actually… taught me
how to cast a single spell, did you?

24:02.357 --> 24:04.734
The only lesson
your pupil has ever learned here

24:04.818 --> 24:07.487
is that his master
had no genuine intention

24:07.571 --> 24:09.322
of ever teaching him real magic at all.

24:09.906 --> 24:12.367
And hence why,
having learned this valuable lesson,

24:12.450 --> 24:14.119
your pupil will be taking his leave.

24:14.619 --> 24:17.831
[monk] The leader of Songrim requested
I keep you here three years.

24:17.914 --> 24:21.126
You're using my training fees
to pay to build the new sanctuary, right?

24:21.209 --> 24:24.171
I will not ask for you to return it,
so I hope it goes well for you.

24:24.254 --> 24:25.630
[Jang Uk clicks tongue, sighs]

24:25.714 --> 24:29.009
[monk] I did not give you permission
to end your training. How dare you?

24:31.094 --> 24:34.598
Do I seem to be…
asking for permission right now?

24:36.725 --> 24:40.520
Conceived by your mother's affair
and abandoned by your father.

24:40.604 --> 24:43.607
I never should have expected you
to understand the bond of duty.

24:43.690 --> 24:46.443
It is I who refuses
to teach a boy like you.

24:46.526 --> 24:47.402
[scoffs]

24:47.485 --> 24:49.654
I may not know much about a pupil's duty,

24:49.738 --> 24:51.364
but I know how to be a creditor.

24:51.448 --> 24:53.074
So, if you try saying another word,

24:53.158 --> 24:55.327
your sanctuary will have
no roof to put on.

24:56.953 --> 24:58.663
As I'll be taking my money back.

24:59.456 --> 25:00.999
It's your father's fault

25:01.082 --> 25:04.211
that no master anywhere would dare
to teach you how to cast spells.

25:04.294 --> 25:06.838
Okay, thank you
for worrying about me, master.

25:07.881 --> 25:11.384
But by myself, I… will find
a master who'll guide me.

25:12.135 --> 25:15.388
Someone skilled and extremely strong.

25:16.473 --> 25:18.475
[upbeat music playing]

25:27.567 --> 25:28.526
- [grunts]
- [birds cawing]

25:32.530 --> 25:34.199
Mu-deok, are you all right?

25:37.953 --> 25:39.287
[indistinct chatter]

25:49.422 --> 25:51.299
[tense music playing]

26:22.747 --> 26:24.749
[light music playing]

26:35.093 --> 26:38.013
[Mu-deok] Of all people,
why did I enter this body?

26:38.638 --> 26:39.514
[yelps]

26:39.597 --> 26:40.849
- [utensils clattering]
- [customer] What's wrong with you?

26:40.932 --> 26:42.809
[Mu-deok] I was certain
that this woman was blind.

26:48.315 --> 26:50.150
So then, why am I able to see?

26:50.775 --> 26:52.610
Is it because our soul shifted bodies?

26:55.280 --> 26:58.116
I can't find the blue mark
of a soul shifter anywhere on her body.

26:58.199 --> 26:59.617
Is it possible?

27:00.660 --> 27:03.747
If you're feeling sick, just hang on!
We're nearly there, Mu-deok.

27:06.291 --> 27:07.250
[Mu-deok] "Mu-deok."

27:07.334 --> 27:10.962
A blind country girl from Sari Village
bought to be sold off in the fortress.

27:14.090 --> 27:15.342
[broker] Sit down. You'll fall.

27:23.183 --> 27:25.185
[epic music playing]

27:26.227 --> 27:27.937
Thanks for getting me here safely.

27:29.064 --> 27:30.065
But I'll be going now.

27:42.494 --> 27:43.703
[Mu-deok] What is wrong with me?

27:44.329 --> 27:45.246
I have no strength.

27:46.456 --> 27:48.875
Is this body so weak
it can't even climb over this?

27:50.043 --> 27:50.877
[grunts]

27:50.960 --> 27:52.128
My arms are shaking.

27:52.212 --> 27:55.256
Mister! Please! Come and help me, please!

27:55.340 --> 27:56.508
What? Mu-deok!

27:56.591 --> 27:58.343
- Mister, please!
- [broker] Oh, what did you do? Just--

27:58.426 --> 28:00.720
- Just hold on! Hold on…
- Please, Mister!

28:00.804 --> 28:03.473
[broker] Turn around!
Turn around! Hurry! Turn around!

28:03.556 --> 28:04.557
- [boatman] What the hell?
- [broker] I'm coming, Mu-deok!

28:04.641 --> 28:06.309
- Jus a little longer!
- [Mu-deok] I'm slipping.

28:06.393 --> 28:07.435
Aargh! Mister!

28:14.484 --> 28:16.277
[roosters crowing]

28:19.364 --> 28:20.990
[broker] Why would someone
who can't even see

28:21.074 --> 28:23.410
try to dangle off a bridge like that?

28:23.493 --> 28:25.245
- You could've gotten hurt.
- [sighs]

28:26.663 --> 28:28.123
[Mu-deok] This is a huge problem.

28:28.206 --> 28:30.041
All of my power is gone.

28:34.337 --> 28:35.422
[retches]

28:35.505 --> 28:37.006
[broker] Motion sickness?

28:37.674 --> 28:40.885
What are we gonna do?
I can't believe how weak you are.

28:41.469 --> 28:42.887
[Mu-deok] He's right. I'm weak!

28:42.971 --> 28:45.014
This body is completely useless.

28:46.099 --> 28:49.686
I'll have to wait to run away
and remain as Mu-deok for now.

28:49.769 --> 28:52.147
I'm very sorry, Mister.

28:52.230 --> 28:53.481
[broker] It is all right.

28:53.565 --> 28:55.316
Just be more careful! You're too frail.

28:55.942 --> 28:57.152
Let's get you something to eat.

29:00.947 --> 29:01.865
[retches]

29:02.991 --> 29:04.033
[groans softly]

29:04.617 --> 29:06.327
- [dog barks]
- [indistinct chatter]

29:09.998 --> 29:11.833
- [woman] Please, enjoy your meal.
- [broker] Yes, thank you.

29:11.916 --> 29:14.711
Come on! Let's eat!
It's chicken. Eat as much as you want.

29:15.462 --> 29:18.298
[Mu-deok] As an assassin,
I must be sensitive to the smell of blood.

29:18.381 --> 29:21.926
Therefore, I can not eat any creature
that sheds blood like a human.

29:22.010 --> 29:24.262
- No, thank you.
- [broker] Just eat.

29:31.519 --> 29:34.272
I've never eaten meat before. It is…

29:35.565 --> 29:36.483
so delicious.

29:36.566 --> 29:38.693
[bird cawing]

29:38.777 --> 29:40.570
[grunts]

29:41.529 --> 29:42.614
Eat up.

29:42.697 --> 29:45.784
Really… really didn't want
to send you there,

29:46.409 --> 29:49.913
but it's the only place that would
take in someone blind like yourself.

29:51.706 --> 29:52.540
What do you mean?

29:53.416 --> 29:54.501
Where's "there"?

29:56.878 --> 29:59.422
[broker] An elderly woman
in Sari Village took her in

29:59.506 --> 30:00.673
after she lost her parents.

30:00.757 --> 30:02.926
But she got sick and passed away.

30:03.009 --> 30:05.470
All of her debt was passed onto this girl,

30:05.553 --> 30:07.472
so that's why she came here to be sold.

30:07.555 --> 30:08.515
I'm off, then.

30:10.016 --> 30:11.768
How could you sell
this unfortunate kid to a brothel?

30:11.851 --> 30:14.229
- I wish you well.
- Wait! Don't…

30:15.480 --> 30:16.314
[grunts angrily]

30:16.397 --> 30:18.191
[Mu-deok]
I can't believe he fed me chicken

30:18.274 --> 30:19.484
just to sell me to this place.

30:19.567 --> 30:22.904
Once I get my strength back, I will
tear you apart like a piece of chicken.

30:22.987 --> 30:24.739
Oh, you are far too skinny.

30:25.240 --> 30:28.076
I wonder if you'd be prettier
if we fattened you up just a bit.

30:28.159 --> 30:30.578
Don't bother. This body can't
possibly get any prettier.

30:31.162 --> 30:33.706
Do you see how ugly I am?
I don't belong in a brothel.

30:33.790 --> 30:35.208
You better just sell me somewhere else.

30:35.291 --> 30:37.418
Well, you're well-spoken.
That's for certain.

30:38.002 --> 30:39.170
I hear that you can sing.

30:39.254 --> 30:41.631
Are you good? As good as you can talk?

30:42.382 --> 30:43.341
[sniffs]

30:44.300 --> 30:46.761
Oh, we'd better wash you first
and dress you up.

30:46.845 --> 30:48.763
[thrilling music playing]

31:01.609 --> 31:03.361
You didn't tell me
that you could dance, too!

31:03.444 --> 31:05.071
You think I'm dancing right now?

31:05.947 --> 31:09.617
[Mu-deok] If I had any power in my steps,
your arm would have been ripped clean off.

31:11.619 --> 31:14.873
You can't speak to your elders
like that. It's really rude!

31:14.956 --> 31:17.458
You'll be in big trouble
if you treat customers like that.

31:17.542 --> 31:19.919
[Mu-deok] Just wait.
I promise I'll kill you.

31:21.129 --> 31:24.966
We have a lot of powerful people
who come and visit our parlor.

31:25.592 --> 31:28.761
The Four Seasons of Daeho
are regulars of Chwiseonru.

31:29.929 --> 31:31.055
The four what?

31:31.139 --> 31:34.434
In Daeho, there are four houses,
each represented by an heir.

31:34.517 --> 31:37.020
And they are known as the Four Seasons.

31:37.103 --> 31:40.064
- [dreamy music playing]
- [birds chirping]

31:50.992 --> 31:53.286
[Ju-wol] There's the daughter
from the Jin family

31:53.369 --> 31:55.371
who has the vitality of spring.

31:55.455 --> 31:56.998
Jin Cho-yeon.

32:03.254 --> 32:05.340
[upbeat music playing]

32:11.429 --> 32:15.433
The heir to the Park family
whose energy is hot like summer.

32:15.516 --> 32:16.726
Park Dang-gu.

32:19.437 --> 32:21.397
[soft music playing]

32:26.986 --> 32:32.033
The genius of the Seo family who is
as noble as the setting sun in fall.

32:32.116 --> 32:33.117
Seo Yul.

32:38.957 --> 32:40.917
[light music playing]

32:50.593 --> 32:54.514
And then, there is
the Jang family's successor

32:54.597 --> 32:58.559
who is as dazzling
as the winter snow, Jang Uk.

33:06.359 --> 33:09.946
The Jin, the Park, the Seo,
and the Jang families are the four

33:10.029 --> 33:12.240
most important mage dynasties
in all of Daeho.

33:12.323 --> 33:14.325
And their children are the Four Seasons.

33:15.410 --> 33:18.079
So do they call them
the Four Seasons inside the fortress?

33:19.122 --> 33:19.956
[Ju-wol gasps]

33:20.039 --> 33:21.916
It looks like
my summer prince is here now!

33:22.000 --> 33:23.084
[chuckles]

33:27.588 --> 33:30.216
[Mu-deok] If he really is
the heir of the Park family,

33:30.299 --> 33:32.593
then he must be
the nephew of Songrim's Park Jin.

33:34.721 --> 33:36.014
Park Jin.

33:36.097 --> 33:37.056
[woman screams]

33:39.642 --> 33:42.603
He was there on that horrible night.

33:44.313 --> 33:46.274
[somber music playing]

33:51.571 --> 33:52.780
The Jin family.

33:53.614 --> 33:54.824
The Seo family.

33:55.366 --> 33:56.576
The Jang family.

33:57.326 --> 33:58.536
The Park family.

34:07.920 --> 34:08.963
The Four Seasons?

34:10.423 --> 34:14.260
Wherever Naksu may go,
you all will be defeated…

34:17.388 --> 34:20.266
beautifully, just like your name.

34:23.227 --> 34:26.481
Was there a particular reason
that you decided to join us today?

34:26.564 --> 34:30.401
My uncle told me
I had to come and get someone.

34:30.985 --> 34:33.154
Get someone? Who is it?

34:33.237 --> 34:35.865
Some trainee who just came from Gisan,

34:35.948 --> 34:38.868
who embarrassed his master
and then was expelled.

34:39.994 --> 34:42.497
I'm certain he's hiding around here.

34:43.164 --> 34:44.999
[Dang-gu clicks tongue]
Oh, well, well, well, well!

34:45.083 --> 34:48.336
That's funny. It seems to me
someone craves seafood…

34:48.419 --> 34:49.462
- [chuckles]
- …after being stuck

34:49.545 --> 34:50.421
in the mountain for so long.

34:50.505 --> 34:52.381
Mm-hmm. That must be his room, then.

34:54.884 --> 34:55.843
[Ju-wol clears throat]

35:01.390 --> 35:02.391
[Dang-gu clears throat]

35:06.938 --> 35:07.897
[exhales deeply]

35:12.151 --> 35:13.152
Wow!

35:14.403 --> 35:16.030
Thanks to all your hard work,

35:16.114 --> 35:18.157
my uncle now has to go
all the way up to Gisan

35:18.241 --> 35:19.742
and beg for that monk's forgiveness.

35:19.826 --> 35:21.869
Meanwhile, you're just
sitting here, all alone,

35:21.953 --> 35:24.580
enjoying this delicious-looking crab.

35:24.664 --> 35:26.290
No, I haven't eaten it yet.

35:26.374 --> 35:27.750
It's too much of a hassle.

35:28.334 --> 35:30.670
You came at the perfect time.
Cast something to break the shell.

35:31.671 --> 35:32.880
Whoa, you…
[laughs softly]

35:32.964 --> 35:34.173
You want to use a violent spell

35:34.257 --> 35:36.968
just so you can rip the crab meat
from its shell. There is one!

35:37.051 --> 35:39.720
But instead of the crab, hmm,
I think I'd rather use it on you.

35:39.804 --> 35:43.224
Dang-gu, if that monk had taught me
a spell to remove a crab shell,

35:43.307 --> 35:45.309
I know that I wouldn't have left
the way I did.

35:45.393 --> 35:47.061
Even if he taught you,
could you actually do it?

35:47.145 --> 35:49.063
I mean, you father still has
your gate of energy blocked.

35:49.147 --> 35:50.731
Then he should have opened it.

35:50.815 --> 35:52.733
That's what masters do
for their students, right?

35:52.817 --> 35:54.318
They need to open what's blocked.

35:54.402 --> 35:57.196
No one in Daeho is
bold enough or brave enough

35:57.280 --> 35:59.323
to even try to go against
your father to open your gate for you.

35:59.407 --> 36:00.992
There are fearless people, though.

36:01.075 --> 36:02.577
For example, there is…
[exhales]

36:03.244 --> 36:05.163
… the Shadow Assassin called Naksu.

36:09.750 --> 36:11.252
Do not be ridiculous.

36:11.335 --> 36:14.005
Are you saying she's not skilled?
Even the leader had a tough time with her.

36:15.298 --> 36:16.632
She is dead, very dead.

36:17.300 --> 36:19.010
I heard that she performed
the alchemy of souls,

36:19.093 --> 36:20.136
so she might be alive.

36:21.596 --> 36:22.930
Uh, where did you hear that from?

36:23.639 --> 36:26.225
Do you really think
I just came here to eat some crab, huh?

36:26.309 --> 36:29.478
Any news in Daeho can be heard
at Chwiseonru before Jeongjingak.

36:30.354 --> 36:31.772
Just crack it open already, will you?

36:31.856 --> 36:33.399
If you already knew the spell

36:33.482 --> 36:34.650
to shelling the crabs,
it's the least you can do.

36:34.734 --> 36:36.027
And you should be able
to pull the crab meat out

36:36.110 --> 36:37.987
with your own hands, right?
You lazy ass!

36:38.070 --> 36:38.988
[dog barks]

36:41.490 --> 36:43.993
You look so pretty now
that you're washed and cleaned up.

36:44.076 --> 36:45.244
I'll do your makeup now.

36:46.454 --> 36:48.956
Thank you, but I can do it myself.

36:49.040 --> 36:50.333
But you can't even see.

36:50.416 --> 36:52.501
Do you really think
you can do it on your own?

36:52.585 --> 36:54.921
[sighs] I've never done anything
like this before,

36:55.004 --> 36:57.131
so I need time to get ready emotionally.

36:58.591 --> 37:00.676
I'd like to be alone for a moment.

37:02.637 --> 37:04.889
Of course! Just come out
when you're ready.

37:12.355 --> 37:13.189
[door opens]

37:15.983 --> 37:18.236
It's a lot easier
to fool people in this woman's body.

37:19.445 --> 37:21.072
To make my escape,
I'll need some money.

37:23.616 --> 37:25.076
Is this real gold?

37:26.619 --> 37:28.120
This one's made of jade.

37:28.955 --> 37:31.540
[Ju-wol] Mu-deok, I want you
to try this new shade.

37:33.668 --> 37:34.543
What are you doing?

37:36.087 --> 37:38.798
Ju-wol, what is wrong?

37:41.384 --> 37:42.969
Can you see me?

37:43.052 --> 37:44.762
[suspenseful music playing]

37:45.805 --> 37:46.639
[shouts]

37:47.807 --> 37:49.141
[grunts, coughs]

37:52.353 --> 37:54.855
Someone go grab her!
Catch that thief!

37:55.564 --> 37:56.565
[groans]

38:00.653 --> 38:01.946
[Mu-deok] It's way too high.

38:07.368 --> 38:08.953
[indistinct chatter]

38:10.288 --> 38:11.205
- [woman laugh]
- [man] Here!

38:34.937 --> 38:36.439
[Jang Uk] What are you looking at?

38:41.027 --> 38:43.029
[soft music playing]

38:54.373 --> 38:55.374
You're…

39:03.299 --> 39:04.425
Don't try to make a sound.

39:06.677 --> 39:09.347
I'd heard that they just
brought a girl who was unable to see.

39:10.014 --> 39:11.057
But you can.

39:14.060 --> 39:15.728
I think I might have heard of your name.

39:15.811 --> 39:17.938
What was it again?
It starts with a D, right?

39:18.022 --> 39:19.106
No! No, it's not!

39:20.441 --> 39:21.650
Oh, that's right!

39:22.568 --> 39:23.444
Mu-deok.

39:25.237 --> 39:27.531
That's right. My name is Mu-deok.

39:28.407 --> 39:30.534
And now that I've gotten
a good look at your face,

39:31.202 --> 39:33.496
if you do not stay quiet
until I get out of here,

39:33.579 --> 39:35.373
I will come back here
and slit your throat.

39:36.415 --> 39:37.249
[Jang Uk scoffs]

39:39.251 --> 39:40.336
What's so funny?

39:42.463 --> 39:43.589
Your beautiful eyes.

39:46.467 --> 39:47.510
Just stop that now!

39:48.636 --> 39:52.056
Uh, sorry. Only your eyes are pretty.

39:53.599 --> 39:54.725
You must be crazy.

40:01.690 --> 40:02.525
[Jang Uk] Mu-deok.

40:03.234 --> 40:04.110
Mu-deok!

40:06.153 --> 40:08.614
Hey, hey! There's not much
to take in there.

40:10.658 --> 40:11.575
Take this!

40:12.868 --> 40:13.869
Take this instead.

40:15.496 --> 40:16.872
- Here!
- [yells]

40:16.956 --> 40:17.998
- Oh, whoa, whoa, whoa, hey…
- [shattering]

40:23.462 --> 40:25.256
[bird cawing]

40:27.299 --> 40:29.468
[indistinct chatter, laughter]

40:33.305 --> 40:34.223
[door opens]

40:34.306 --> 40:35.391
[scoffs]

40:37.685 --> 40:40.312
- What are you looking at? Huh?
- Nothing.

40:45.693 --> 40:46.652
Park Dang-gu.

40:48.362 --> 40:51.115
I heard the Shadow Assassin,
Naksu, used Tansu to fight.

40:51.198 --> 40:53.117
[scoffs]
Do you even know what Tansu is?

40:53.200 --> 40:55.703
Mm, yes, I read a bit about it.

40:56.203 --> 40:57.121
TANSU

40:57.830 --> 40:59.165
[Dang-gu] Tansu, you see,

40:59.248 --> 41:02.793
is a style of swordsmanship that only
the best mages can attempt to practice.

41:02.877 --> 41:05.838
Just like you can flick water,
you can flick your energy with your blade.

41:05.921 --> 41:08.382
Even a single move
could be enough to end your life.

41:10.509 --> 41:12.386
[upbeat music playing]

41:18.309 --> 41:20.060
Wait, hold on.
Why do you ask?

41:21.145 --> 41:22.396
I was wondering whether or not

41:22.480 --> 41:24.607
I almost got killed
by this crab like just now.

41:24.690 --> 41:27.526
Ah, give it here!
Come on! Give it, I'll de-shell it for--

41:29.069 --> 41:32.198
Hey, Jang Uk, that's a critical hit.

41:33.782 --> 41:35.034
That's my vital point.

41:35.117 --> 41:37.328
In one move, she aimed at my vital point.

41:38.662 --> 41:39.497
[Dang-gu exhales]

41:40.414 --> 41:41.916
- But that's it.
- [exhales]

41:41.999 --> 41:43.834
Then why did she fall off?

41:43.918 --> 41:45.544
[crowd chattering]

41:48.547 --> 41:51.091
[Mu-deok] How is it that
this tiny body is always so hungry, 

41:51.175 --> 41:52.426
no matter how much I eat?

41:52.510 --> 41:54.678
I'll only get weak if I let myself starve.

41:55.179 --> 41:56.555
Guess there's no choice, then.

41:56.639 --> 41:57.473
Ah!

41:58.599 --> 41:59.725
[rooster crowing]

42:01.477 --> 42:02.394
[exhales angrily]

42:03.020 --> 42:04.480
[lion roars]

42:07.274 --> 42:09.860
Now is not the time to fight. Keep it in.
[clears throat]

42:15.366 --> 42:17.576
[male seller] Look! It's mages
from Jeongjingak.

42:17.660 --> 42:19.662
[thrilling music playing]

42:24.833 --> 42:26.919
I heard that an assassin entered
Songrim Jeongjingak.

42:27.002 --> 42:28.921
[man 1] I heard that she was
after the leader, but was killed.

42:29.004 --> 42:30.756
- [woman gasps]
- [man 2] The assassin is a young woman.

42:30.839 --> 42:32.132
[female seller] Oh, my!

42:39.014 --> 42:40.975
[romantic music playing]

43:04.039 --> 43:06.000
[Mu-deok] He must have
already seen my dead body.

43:06.542 --> 43:08.294
He wouldn't recognize me anyway.

43:09.128 --> 43:10.087
That whistle…

43:10.713 --> 43:12.506
he wouldn't have remembered that either.

43:15.801 --> 43:19.138
[menacing music playing]

43:22.141 --> 43:24.602
[Gil-ju] There's no sign that
Naksu travelled through here.

43:25.561 --> 43:28.355
However, it seems like
she failed to shift souls.

43:29.440 --> 43:32.192
[Jin Mu] Even if she were to succeed,
she's probably in hiding

43:32.276 --> 43:34.570
because she encountered a problem.

43:34.653 --> 43:37.448
An assassin whose identity
has been revealed must be forsaken.

43:39.908 --> 43:41.785
We need to retrieve her body and sword.

43:41.869 --> 43:44.204
Destroy any trace of Naksu
that's left behind.

43:44.288 --> 43:48.250
[Gil-ju] If somehow she's still alive,
what should I do, then?

43:49.793 --> 43:52.212
[Jin Mu] She'll either be found
as a soul shifter and killed,

43:52.296 --> 43:56.258
or she'll run wild as her soul
and new body clash until she is stoned.

43:56.842 --> 43:59.136
I trained her to become
the ultimate assassin.

44:00.471 --> 44:01.430
What a pity!

44:06.185 --> 44:07.061
[sighs]

44:07.770 --> 44:08.646
[Mu-deok clicks tongue]

44:09.813 --> 44:11.398
How much more do you need to study it?

44:11.482 --> 44:15.444
These are pricey.
I need to inspect them closely.

44:15.527 --> 44:18.822
I don't need much money for it.
Just pay me a rough estimate, okay?

44:21.200 --> 44:22.076
[male merchant] Right over here!

44:22.993 --> 44:24.578
- This is her! Take her!
- What…

44:24.662 --> 44:25.954
[male merchant] Get her out of here.

44:27.373 --> 44:28.207
[man screams]

44:35.631 --> 44:36.674
[gasps]

44:36.757 --> 44:38.175
[ominous music playing]

44:41.428 --> 44:44.556
[Mu-deok] Where am I?
Did they realize who I am?

44:45.140 --> 44:46.558
So, then, is this Songrim?

44:49.895 --> 44:51.271
Are you finally awake?

44:51.355 --> 44:53.691
Who are you? And where am I?

44:57.736 --> 45:00.656
The home of Master Jang Gang,
the Gwanju of Cheonbugwan.

45:01.240 --> 45:04.118
[Mu-deok] "Jang Gang"?
This is the house of the Jang family?

45:08.831 --> 45:12.292
I don't know why the Young Master
decided to bring someone so frail-looking

45:12.376 --> 45:13.293
into this house.

45:13.377 --> 45:15.879
- "Young Master"?
- That's right.

45:15.963 --> 45:17.798
Young Master Uk
of this house paid the brothel

45:17.881 --> 45:19.758
before bringing you back home with him.

45:19.842 --> 45:21.260
I heard that you…

45:21.343 --> 45:23.387
stole from the Young Master
at the brothel. Is that so?

45:25.389 --> 45:26.432
[Jang Uk] Take this instead.

45:27.891 --> 45:29.935
- [yelps]
- Oh, whoa, whoa, whoa, hey!

45:30.894 --> 45:32.521
[Mu-deok] What does he want with me?

45:32.604 --> 45:35.607
I was quite worried when he said he was
bringing a girl home from the brothel.

45:36.233 --> 45:38.026
But now that I've seen you, I care less.

45:38.110 --> 45:39.778
He just brought you here out of pity.

45:40.571 --> 45:41.405
Here.

45:41.905 --> 45:42.865
Go! Get changed!

45:42.948 --> 45:44.158
Mu-deok, now.

45:44.241 --> 45:46.243
- What the hell is this?
- Really?

45:46.326 --> 45:48.120
Your uniform as
the Young Master's servant.

45:48.203 --> 45:52.249
Also, how dare you speak
like that to your elder, young lady!

45:53.041 --> 45:55.419
[scoffs]
Young Master is very frail,

45:55.502 --> 45:57.254
so he gets tired very easily.

45:57.337 --> 46:00.299
So you need to do your tasks
as soon as the Young Master requests them.

46:00.382 --> 46:03.927
And also, regardless of what
he says to you, always smile.

46:05.137 --> 46:06.221
Do you understand me?

46:07.389 --> 46:08.223
Yes.

46:09.141 --> 46:09.975
Good.

46:10.058 --> 46:13.479
He wanted to see you as soon as
you woke up, so go get changed quickly.

46:13.562 --> 46:14.646
Understand?

46:15.355 --> 46:16.190
Yes…

46:17.649 --> 46:18.484
Missus.

46:20.152 --> 46:22.070
Please call me "ma'am",
nothing other than that.

46:26.492 --> 46:27.576
"The Young Master"?

46:28.994 --> 46:30.454
Why would he bring me here?

46:33.665 --> 46:34.750
Your beautiful eyes…

46:36.126 --> 46:37.377
Did he fall for me?

46:37.461 --> 46:38.962
[whimsical music playing]

46:39.046 --> 46:40.172
For this ugly face?

46:41.089 --> 46:41.965
[scoffs]

46:42.049 --> 46:44.259
He has such a terrible taste.
[clicks tongue]

46:51.350 --> 46:53.393
[Mu-deok] Regardless,
until I can regain my power,

46:53.477 --> 46:55.896
it might be safer if I just hide out here.

46:57.523 --> 47:01.568
If he really has fallen for this body,
at least I'll be treated well.

47:02.736 --> 47:03.862
So, then…

47:04.404 --> 47:08.200
at least while I'm here,
I will be Mu-deok.

47:09.576 --> 47:12.454
Young Master. Mu-deok is here.

47:13.455 --> 47:14.289
[Jang Uk] Come in.

47:18.961 --> 47:20.921
[dramatic music playing]

47:25.634 --> 47:26.552
[Mu-deok] Young Master.

47:26.635 --> 47:28.679
I wanted to thank you
so much for saving my life.

47:28.762 --> 47:31.181
Thank you for bringing me here.

47:32.182 --> 47:34.309
It only took a few ordinary men
to drag you over here.

47:36.061 --> 47:38.689
- That's disappointing.
- I know that it was very rude of me

47:38.772 --> 47:40.899
to threaten you the way
I did with that crab leg,

47:41.733 --> 47:42.859
but please forgive me for it.

47:42.943 --> 47:44.444
You found some manners, I see!

47:44.528 --> 47:46.572
I'll serve you the best
that I possibly can.

47:47.281 --> 47:48.782
Fine, you go do your best.

47:48.865 --> 47:51.243
Mu-deok, go and fetch me
some water, please.

47:51.994 --> 47:53.161
Yes, Young Master.

47:54.788 --> 47:55.622
[door opens]

48:00.419 --> 48:01.253
Hang on.

48:01.878 --> 48:03.755
Not drinking water, washing water.

48:04.506 --> 48:06.592
Ah, yes, Young Master.

48:11.138 --> 48:13.390
Instead of washing my face,
I'll just take a bath.

48:20.105 --> 48:21.481
[groans]
Hot, hot!

48:21.565 --> 48:23.525
Gosh, this is far too hot!

48:25.193 --> 48:26.612
Yes, Young Master.

48:32.909 --> 48:34.411
Oh. It's cold.

48:34.995 --> 48:36.288
It's a bit too cold.

48:39.875 --> 48:41.043
It doesn't feel cold.

48:41.126 --> 48:43.503
It is. I'll get sick if I bathe in this.

48:45.339 --> 48:47.049
- [Mu-deok] What's with this asshole?
- It's freezing.

48:47.132 --> 48:48.383
[Mu-deok] Is he not in love with me?

48:48.467 --> 48:49.926
What? Are you gonna fix it?

48:51.136 --> 48:52.220
Yes, Young Master.

48:52.304 --> 48:54.348
- I'll get some hot water.
- [cat meows]

49:00.187 --> 49:01.021
Salty.

49:01.104 --> 49:04.524
Oh! Too sweet. So spicy.
Too long. What is this thing?

49:04.608 --> 49:05.817
I won't eat this.

49:06.318 --> 49:07.152
[chuckles softly]

49:09.321 --> 49:11.031
This water smells kinda strange.

49:11.740 --> 49:12.658
Does it smell?

49:13.659 --> 49:14.951
Bring me a new bucket.

49:16.453 --> 49:17.954
[sighs]

49:18.038 --> 49:19.748
I'll need a different blanket.

49:20.415 --> 49:22.209
I feel like I'll sleep better
with the blue blanket tonight.

49:24.002 --> 49:25.921
[whimsical music playing]

49:26.004 --> 49:26.922
[sighs]

49:44.481 --> 49:46.191
He doesn't even do a damn thing all day,

49:46.274 --> 49:48.443
and yet he still needs
to take three baths a day.

49:50.946 --> 49:51.780
[exhales]

49:52.364 --> 49:53.532
I will kill him.

49:53.615 --> 49:57.244
When I regain my energy, he's going
to be the first person that I kill.

50:01.415 --> 50:03.917
Young Master, I brought you cold water.

50:04.710 --> 50:05.544
I have it here.

50:05.627 --> 50:07.337
Oh, good. The water finally cooled.

50:07.421 --> 50:08.880
Ah, just right!

50:08.964 --> 50:09.798
[thuds]

50:10.340 --> 50:11.425
Great job…

50:11.508 --> 50:13.885
No, hold on! I was pointless, Mu-deok.

50:13.969 --> 50:15.053
[Jang Uk laughs]

50:15.595 --> 50:16.596
[Jang Uk yawns]

50:20.976 --> 50:22.853
[ominous music playing]

50:25.063 --> 50:26.481
[Mu-deok] If I had my power…

50:27.274 --> 50:30.527
if I had even a tenth of my energy
coursing through these hands…

50:44.583 --> 50:47.669
Hold on! What?
What… what is happening?

50:48.170 --> 50:49.254
[groaning]

50:51.631 --> 50:52.716
[yells]

50:58.513 --> 50:59.681
[coughs]

51:04.811 --> 51:06.021
[Jang Uk] Something funny?

51:07.439 --> 51:08.356
What?

51:09.399 --> 51:11.026
Why are you smiling at me like that, huh?

51:11.985 --> 51:13.111
It's nothing, Young Master.

51:13.195 --> 51:14.780
The water's refreshing.
[chuckles]

51:15.739 --> 51:17.032
My clothes!

51:17.115 --> 51:18.366
Yes, Young Master.

51:20.285 --> 51:21.411
[sighs]

51:21.495 --> 51:22.329
[Jang Uk clears throat]

51:27.292 --> 51:28.710
What are you doing?

51:29.252 --> 51:30.587
Oh, here you go.

51:33.548 --> 51:35.509
You can go. That's enough for today.

51:36.092 --> 51:37.219
Yes, Young Master.

51:49.189 --> 51:50.690
That was definitely a Spirit Plaque

51:50.774 --> 51:53.276
that could allow me to open
the barrier and enter Songrim.

51:55.195 --> 51:56.822
But I can't cast spells to help me break

51:56.905 --> 51:58.949
the barrier into Songrim
in my current state.

52:00.617 --> 52:02.160
[Mu-deok] I should find my sword.

52:03.411 --> 52:06.331
My power might return
if I can hold my sword.

52:09.668 --> 52:11.127
If I had the Spirit Plaque,

52:12.087 --> 52:14.631
nothing can stop me
from entering into Songrim now.

52:19.302 --> 52:22.639
SONGRIM

52:23.765 --> 52:27.060
[Sang-ho] So, how long do you plan on
keeping Naksu's body here?

52:27.727 --> 52:29.813
If she somehow successfully shifted souls,

52:30.355 --> 52:31.189
Naksu…

52:32.440 --> 52:33.859
will come to get her sword.

52:35.610 --> 52:38.905
Since her body is here,
she will surely come.

52:40.198 --> 52:42.117
So just wait and watch for the time being.

52:48.957 --> 52:52.252
[maid Kim] Maybe it's just because
your father's room is always empty,

52:52.919 --> 52:54.546
but it never seems to get dusty.

52:55.797 --> 52:57.382
I wonder when he'll come back.

53:01.386 --> 53:04.848
The color in your mother's portrait
has faded quite a bit.

53:05.473 --> 53:07.517
We should call
for a painter to touch it up.

53:22.824 --> 53:24.826
[somber music playing]

53:30.624 --> 53:33.084
[young Jang Uk] I have memorized
every single book you told me to read.

53:33.668 --> 53:35.128
So, just like you and Dang-gu,

53:35.754 --> 53:37.756
please, let me study spells at Songrim.

53:45.972 --> 53:49.184
That sword there,
it belongs to your father.

53:49.267 --> 53:50.560
Now, take it out.

54:01.446 --> 54:02.697
[wind howling]

54:03.698 --> 54:05.325
But my gate of energy is blocked,

54:05.867 --> 54:08.119
I'm not able to unsheathe
a sword that has a spell on it.

54:08.870 --> 54:11.122
How can you expect
to learn how to cast any spells

54:11.206 --> 54:12.874
when you can't even unsheathe
your father's sword?

54:12.958 --> 54:15.835
As Songrim's leader,
can't you just open my gate of energy?

54:15.919 --> 54:16.836
[Jin] No!

54:18.046 --> 54:19.422
I can't do that.

54:20.799 --> 54:21.633
Then…

54:22.509 --> 54:24.219
please go find me a new master that can.

54:24.928 --> 54:26.304
No master will ever help.

54:27.180 --> 54:29.557
There is no mage in Daeho
that would go against your father

54:29.641 --> 54:31.726
and dare to open
your gate of energy for you.

54:31.810 --> 54:33.144
Then what you're telling me…

54:34.229 --> 54:36.106
that it's impossible
for me, no matter what?

54:36.189 --> 54:38.775
That is the fate that your father…

54:39.734 --> 54:41.403
has determined for you.

54:42.362 --> 54:43.697
[young Jang Uk] That's not fair!

54:44.322 --> 54:46.116
Why does he get to decide my future?

54:47.492 --> 54:49.869
No one even considers him
to be my father, anyway!

54:51.413 --> 54:52.622
I will find someone.

54:53.957 --> 54:57.752
A master who's willing to open up
my gate of energy and teach me.

54:58.795 --> 55:00.547
I will find someone on my own.

55:01.965 --> 55:04.342
And unsheathe that sword
so I can break it in half.

55:07.595 --> 55:09.597
[somber music playing]

55:31.036 --> 55:33.079
[woman 1] I heard that
Uk was expelled again.

55:33.163 --> 55:36.291
How can the son of the great Lord
get away with behaving like that?

55:37.000 --> 55:38.293
Well, he's not his real son.

55:38.793 --> 55:41.629
I heard his mother,
the most beautiful woman in Daeho,

55:41.713 --> 55:44.174
slept with another man before Uk was born.

55:44.257 --> 55:45.675
[woman 2] I doubt that's true.

55:45.759 --> 55:49.137
[woman 1] Why not? Why else would he
block his own son's gate of energy

55:49.220 --> 55:50.680
and then run away?

55:51.973 --> 55:55.769
Did his father really do something to him?

56:05.737 --> 56:07.697
[Mu-deok] The Spirit Plaque should be
here somewhere.

56:22.003 --> 56:22.921
Where is it?

56:24.798 --> 56:26.800
[suspenseful music playing]

56:48.822 --> 56:50.782
Am I stupid? Why did I hide here?

56:50.865 --> 56:52.158
What will he think if he sees me?

56:53.660 --> 56:54.619
What will I say to him?

57:01.126 --> 57:03.795
I didn't bring you into my service
with this in mind.

57:05.797 --> 57:06.631
Well, uh…

57:07.298 --> 57:09.300
you kept telling me
how cold you were, Young Master.

57:09.384 --> 57:11.636
I thought that I could
warm up the bed for you.

57:12.137 --> 57:15.014
If you lay down right now, you can sleep
soundly as you'll be warm all night.

57:15.098 --> 57:16.307
Oh, really?

57:16.808 --> 57:17.767
Oh!
[chuckles]

57:17.851 --> 57:19.018
That was kind of you.

57:19.644 --> 57:20.562
[nervous chuckle]

57:23.481 --> 57:25.650
- Well, good night, then.
- Where are you going?

57:27.819 --> 57:29.195
You said you would
keep me warm, didn't you?

57:30.947 --> 57:31.823
Keep my bed

57:32.866 --> 57:34.033
nice and hot…

57:35.368 --> 57:36.286
all night.

57:38.580 --> 57:39.747
Warm it up.

57:44.002 --> 57:46.546
[Mu-deok] What?
Is he really in love with me?

57:47.255 --> 57:48.840
Did I fall into his trap?

57:57.265 --> 57:58.099
Young Master…

57:59.058 --> 58:01.644
my body won't produce
enough heat to keep you warm.

58:01.728 --> 58:03.730
Ever since I was a child,
I easily get cold.

58:03.813 --> 58:06.232
So my body is always unbearably frigid.

58:13.573 --> 58:14.782
[Jang Uk exhales]

58:16.576 --> 58:18.578
[upbeat music playing]

58:28.421 --> 58:31.424
I refuse to do whatever sick thing
you're trying to get me to do.

58:41.309 --> 58:43.686
Could you just bring
the brazier over here already?

58:47.565 --> 58:48.733
The brazier?

58:48.816 --> 58:52.362
Yeah, I just want you to bring
the brazier, so it's right next to my bed,

58:52.445 --> 58:53.530
so I stay warm.

58:55.698 --> 58:56.658
Oh.

58:57.867 --> 58:58.785
Stay warm.

59:04.749 --> 59:05.875
[Naksu clears throat]

59:05.959 --> 59:06.834
Here you go.

59:07.418 --> 59:09.212
Hey, if it's that close, it will be too…

59:10.630 --> 59:12.090
It will get too hot, right?

59:12.882 --> 59:14.968
Ah, oh, way… way too hot.

59:17.637 --> 59:18.972
[sighs]

59:19.055 --> 59:20.765
Stay there
and keep the fire going all night.

59:20.848 --> 59:22.517
I promise I'll sell you if it goes out.

59:22.600 --> 59:23.726
Yes, Young Master.

59:31.317 --> 59:32.277
[exhales]

59:35.613 --> 59:38.825
Hey! All right, all right.
Dang-gu is here.

59:42.453 --> 59:44.664
[exhales]
What is that? Oh, it's a whistle.

59:45.373 --> 59:46.249
[Seo Yul] Mm.

59:47.208 --> 59:48.876
I believe that I actually made this.

59:48.960 --> 59:52.171
Oh, that's right, that's right.
You had a pet bird, right?

59:52.255 --> 59:54.090
Are you getting a new one?

59:55.341 --> 59:58.261
No, not that. I just found it
with someone I didn't expect.

59:59.804 --> 01:00:01.431
I wonder why she ended up with it.

01:00:02.056 --> 01:00:03.349
[Dang-gu] Did you give it to her?

01:00:03.933 --> 01:00:06.019
Hey, maybe you just forgot all about it.

01:00:06.102 --> 01:00:07.186
Can't be.

01:00:08.062 --> 01:00:10.231
I clearly remember
the person that I gave this to.

01:00:11.357 --> 01:00:13.318
[soft music playing]

01:00:27.457 --> 01:00:30.251
Well, then, just go and ask her.

01:00:37.467 --> 01:00:39.844
[stutters]
Are you really going to do it right now?

01:00:39.927 --> 01:00:41.262
I need a closer look at something.

01:00:52.690 --> 01:00:54.692
[suspenseful music playing]

01:01:39.320 --> 01:01:41.155
[suspenseful music continues playing]

01:02:27.952 --> 01:02:29.954
[tense music playing]

01:02:36.586 --> 01:02:38.045
Who are these people?

01:02:53.603 --> 01:02:54.437
[man] Stop!

01:02:55.730 --> 01:02:56.773
We have intruders!

01:02:57.523 --> 01:02:58.816
Intruders!

01:03:13.706 --> 01:03:15.166
[swords clanking]

01:03:17.043 --> 01:03:17.877
[attacker grunts]

01:03:20.087 --> 01:03:22.089
[action music playing]

01:03:37.980 --> 01:03:39.357
- [attacker yelps]
- [Dang-gu exclaims]

01:03:57.250 --> 01:03:58.167
Go back.

01:04:02.463 --> 01:04:03.840
[swords whooshing]

01:04:20.982 --> 01:04:22.525
[all clamoring]

01:04:29.532 --> 01:04:30.616
Step aside!

01:04:50.636 --> 01:04:52.430
[dramatic music playing]

01:05:11.157 --> 01:05:12.241
[Dang-gu] Yul.

01:05:12.825 --> 01:05:13.743
What's going on here?

01:05:17.330 --> 01:05:19.373
The Training Center has been set on fire.

01:05:26.756 --> 01:05:28.466
Is there anyone at Jeongjingak now?

01:05:28.549 --> 01:05:30.051
Master Yul and Dang-gu
should still be there.

01:05:33.262 --> 01:05:34.639
Uncle Jin, are you okay?

01:05:35.848 --> 01:05:37.642
The intruders have all fled from here.

01:05:39.226 --> 01:05:40.937
So, Jeongjingak is empty.

01:05:44.690 --> 01:05:46.192
[footsteps approaching]

01:05:51.614 --> 01:05:53.032
- Go after them.
- [all] Sir!

01:06:03.709 --> 01:06:04.919
[Mu-deok] Who were those men?

01:06:06.212 --> 01:06:08.130
Did the Danju send them here?

01:06:10.091 --> 01:06:11.717
[Mu] The one whose soul you must collect

01:06:11.801 --> 01:06:14.595
this time is Park Jin,
the leader of Songrim.

01:06:18.391 --> 01:06:19.308
Right.

01:06:20.601 --> 01:06:22.853
The Danju must have sent them
to come get my body.

01:06:28.693 --> 01:06:29.568
[objects clacking]

01:06:30.653 --> 01:06:31.487
Who is there?

01:06:32.029 --> 01:06:33.990
[suspenseful music playing]

01:07:03.227 --> 01:07:04.228
[breathes heavily]

01:07:05.146 --> 01:07:06.022
Young Master?

01:07:06.105 --> 01:07:07.314
[shushes]

01:07:20.453 --> 01:07:21.704
What are you doing here?

01:07:25.291 --> 01:07:26.417
Because of your eyes.

01:07:27.585 --> 01:07:28.461
Eyes?

01:07:28.544 --> 01:07:30.546
[soft music playing]

01:07:51.150 --> 01:07:52.443
I knew you'd be my master…

01:07:55.613 --> 01:07:56.781
as soon as I saw that.

01:07:56.864 --> 01:08:00.242
[closing theme music playing]

01:08:40.616 --> 01:08:43.994
[Jang Uk] A soul shifter.
The Shadow Assassin, Naksu.

01:08:44.078 --> 01:08:46.247
I have been searching all over
to find the greatest master to serve.

01:08:46.330 --> 01:08:48.290
The one who'll open my gate of energy.

01:08:48.374 --> 01:08:49.917
I want you to be my master.

01:08:50.000 --> 01:08:51.627
I would never have imagined such nonsense.

01:08:51.710 --> 01:08:54.672
One of Naksu's men is in here.
They're going to catch him.

01:08:54.755 --> 01:08:58.634
As of now,
we'll seek out that soul shifter.

01:08:59.343 --> 01:09:01.345
Pretend you know nothing,
even if they catch me.

01:09:02.638 --> 01:09:04.390
Stay right by my side.

01:09:05.057 --> 01:09:06.851
[Mu-deok] Throughout my life,
I've only met those

01:09:06.934 --> 01:09:08.018
who have wanted me dead.

01:09:09.311 --> 01:09:13.232
You are the first person
who's ever tried… to save my life.

01:09:13.899 --> 01:09:16.152
Even if you come this close to me again,

01:09:16.235 --> 01:09:18.195
I promise I will spare you.
